---
export const prerender = true;
import BaseLayout from '../components/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Access Free Tools"
  description="Read the Access Free Tools privacy policy, including browser-first tools, cookies, local preferences, advertising, affiliate links, and user choices."
  path="/privacy-policy/"
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Privacy Policy</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>
      Access Free Tools is designed to keep browser utilities fast, clear, and privacy-aware.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section content-section-narrow legal-copy">
    <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> September 13, 2026</p>

    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>
      This policy explains how Access Free Tools handles information when you use our
      calculators, converters, blog guides, advertising, affiliate links, and other site features.
      It is written for the public website at accessfreetools.com.
    </p>

    <h2>Browser-first tools</h2>
    <p>
      Most tools run in your browser. Calculator history, random number results, and similar
      temporary tool outputs stay in the current browser tab while you use the page and are not
      sent to a server by these tools.
    </p>

    <h2>Browser text-to-speech MP3 pilot</h2>
    <p>
      The text-to-speech pilot reads pasted text or a TXT file you open locally, runs the speech
      model, and creates MP3 audio inside your browser. Access Free Tools does not receive or store
      the text, the local filename, or generated audio. The temporary generated-audio URL disappears
      when the browser tab is closed or refreshed. Fixed voice samples contain only a public comparison
      sentence and do not use text you enter.
    </p>
    <p>
      After you choose to load the model, the browser downloads pinned model and voice files from
      Hugging Face. Those requests can expose ordinary network request information to Hugging Face,
      but they do not contain your text. The pilot records only bounded, text-free actions such as
      voice sample played, model ready, generation complete, cancellation, download, timeout, model-download
      failure, unsupported browser, and generation failure.
    </p>

    <h2>Information we may collect</h2>
    <p>
      We do not currently offer user accounts or payment checkout on Access Free Tools. We may
      receive basic technical information through hosting, security, browser requests, and
      privacy-aware analytics, such as browser type, device type, pages visited, tool actions,
      referring pages, dates, approximate technical request details, and session-quality signals.
      This helps keep the site working, secure, and useful.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you use the contact form, we receive the name, email address, topic, and message you
      choose to submit. The form sends that message to our site email so we can read it and reply.
      Do not submit passwords, bank details, medical records, or other sensitive personal
      information.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
    <p>
      The color look you choose is saved in your browser's local storage so the site can remember
      your preferred style on future visits. You can clear it by clearing site data in your browser.
    </p>
    <p>
      We use local storage to remember an anonymous visitor ID and session storage for an anonymous
      tab-session ID used by simple first-party analytics. This helps us see which tools are actually
      used, how many visitors are new or returning, and which pages need improvement. Analytics page
      paths do not include query strings or fragments. We do not save raw IP addresses in the
      analytics event log; technical request details are hashed or summarized before storage.
    </p>
    <p>
      Advertising, affiliate tracking, third-party analytics, or consent tools may use cookies, web
      beacons, local storage, IP addresses, device identifiers, or similar technologies. You can
      usually control cookies in your browser settings, but some site features may work less
      smoothly if cookies or local storage are disabled.
    </p>

    <h2>First-party analytics</h2>
    <p>
      Access Free Tools may collect simple first-party analytics events, such as page views and tool
      actions like calculate, convert, generate, copy, or check. These events are used to understand
      which tools are useful, spot broken pages, improve internal links, and decide what to build
      next. We filter obvious bots and do not use this system to sell personal profiles.
    </p>

    <h2>Ask tool routing</h2>
    <p>
      When you use Ask Access Free Tools, the question you type may be sent to our hosted
      language-model provider so the service can select the most suitable Access Free Tools
      utility. The selected calculation or conversion is then run by deterministic tool code. Do
      not enter passwords, financial account details, medical records, or other sensitive
      information into Ask.
    </p>

    <h2>Microsoft Clarity</h2>
    <p>
      We use Microsoft Clarity on public site pages to understand how people move through the site,
      where pages are confusing, and whether layouts or tools are hard to use. Clarity may collect
      interaction data such as clicks, scrolling, page visits, device/browser details, and session
      replay signals under Microsoft's privacy terms.
    </p>
    <p>
      Access Free Tools does not load Clarity on private admin or private analytics pages. The site
      also avoids loading Clarity when the browser has Do Not Track enabled or when this browser has
      the Access Free Tools analytics opt-out set in local storage.
    </p>
    <p>
      Text, local-file, filename, model-status, voice-sample, and generated-audio surfaces in the
      text-to-speech pilot are masked from Clarity. We record only bounded, text-free events needed
      to understand whether the pilot works.
    </p>

    <h2>Clipboard actions</h2>
    <p>
      Some tools include copy buttons. These only write the result you choose to your device
      clipboard after you press the copy button.
    </p>

    <h2 id="advertising">Advertising and Infolinks</h2>
    <p>
      Infolinks advertising is not active because our publisher application was not approved.
      Its script does not load, including for visitors who previously allowed ads. If approved and
      enabled later with the required consent, InText could mark selected words with a double underline
      and show a sponsored ad. Infolinks and its advertising partners could then
      receive browser, device, network, approximate location, page, cookie, and ad-interaction data
      under their own policies.
    </p>
    <p>
      We use Infolinks' supported page-boundary controls to keep its scanner out of private admin
      pages, APIs, tool inputs and results, Ask messages, contact forms, navigation, and the footer.
      Infolinks does not receive the private text protected inside those areas through this
      integration.
    </p>
    <p>
      Read the <a href="https://sites0001.infolinks.com/privacy-policy" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">Infolinks
      Privacy Policy</a>. You can also use the <a href="https://optout.networkadvertising.org/" rel="noreferrer"
      target="_blank">Network Advertising Initiative opt-out</a> or, where relevant, <a
      href="https://www.youronlinechoices.com/" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">Your Online Choices</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Google AdSense status</h2>
    <p>
      Google AdSense ads are not active. They will stay off until the account is approved, exact
      publisher and slot identifiers are configured, and a Google-certified consent platform is
      ready where required. If that changes, this policy will be updated before ads are enabled.
    </p>
    <p>
      If AdSense is enabled later, the following applies. Third-party vendors, including Google, may
      use cookies to serve ads based on earlier visits to this or other websites. You can learn about
      Google's use of advertising cookies and review choices in <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noreferrer"
      target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>. Additional industry choices are available at <a
      href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">aboutads.info</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>EEA, UK, and Switzerland consent</h2>
    <p>
      Infolinks is currently disabled for all visitors. Google advertising,
      if enabled later, will require a Google-certified Consent Management Platform for users in the
      European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, and Switzerland where required. Advertising stays
      off when a supported Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track signal is present.
    </p>

    <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
    <p>
      Some future blog guides or product callouts may include affiliate links to third-party stores,
      such as print-on-demand products related to a tool. If you click an affiliate link and buy
      something, Access Free Tools may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. Affiliate partners
      may use their own cookies or tracking links and handle your information under their own privacy
      policies.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party links and services</h2>
    <p>
      Our pages may link to third-party websites, ad networks, affiliate stores, documentation,
      source references, or product pages. We do not control those third-party services, and their
      privacy practices may be different from ours.
    </p>

    <h2>Google Preferred Sources</h2>
    <p>
      Indexable blog articles load Google's official Preferred Sources button from
      <code>news.google.com</code>. Loading the button may send ordinary request information, such as
      browser and network details, to Google. If you use the button or its settings link, Google
      handles your source preference under Google's privacy terms. The button does not receive text
      or results entered into Access Free Tools utilities.
    </p>

    <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Access Free Tools is not designed to knowingly collect personal information from children
      under 13. If you believe a child has provided personal information to us, contact us so we can
      review and remove it where appropriate.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      Advertising is currently disabled, regardless of any advertising preference saved earlier.
      Choose <strong>Ad choices</strong> in the footer to read the current status. You can also
      clear local storage and cookies, use the industry opt-out links above, avoid clicking ads or
      affiliate links, or contact us with privacy questions. If a form asks for personal
      information, submit only what is needed for that request.
    </p>
    <div class="analytics-opt-out-actions" aria-label="Access Free Tools analytics preference">
      <button class="button-primary" type="button" data-public-analytics-choice="out">
        Exclude this browser
      </button>
      <button class="button-secondary" type="button" data-public-analytics-choice="in">
        Count this browser again
      </button>
    </div>
    <p class="analytics-opt-out-status" data-public-analytics-status aria-live="polite">
      Checking this browser's analytics preference...
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy questions, use the <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page or email
      <a href="mailto:contact@accessfreetools.com">contact@accessfreetools.com</a>.
      This policy should be reviewed before new analytics, advertising, affiliate, account, or form
      features go live.
    </p>
  </section>

  <script is:inline>
    (() => {
      const key = 'access-free-tools-analytics-opt-out';
      const status = document.querySelector('[data-public-analytics-status]');

      const updateStatus = () => {
        const optedOut = window.localStorage.getItem(key) === 'true';
        if (status) {
          status.textContent = optedOut
            ? 'This browser is excluded from Access Free Tools first-party analytics and Microsoft Clarity.'
            : 'This browser is currently counted by Access Free Tools analytics.';
        }
      };

      document.querySelectorAll('[data-public-analytics-choice]').forEach((button) => {
        button.addEventListener('click', () => {
          if (button.getAttribute('data-public-analytics-choice') === 'out') {
            window.localStorage.setItem(key, 'true');
          } else {
            window.localStorage.removeItem(key);
          }
          updateStatus();
          window.location.reload();
        });
      });

      updateStatus();
    })();
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
